# =============================================================================
# geometry/molaro/molaro_2D_L387um_eps0.35um_axisym_T-20pair_tangent.opts
#
# The committed -20 C Molaro grain pair, restarted FROM TANGENT CONTACT instead
# of from a pre-formed neck. Pair with
# experiment/molaro/molaro_T-20_h1.00_8h_a1.34e-2.opts.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
# ---------------
# Every existing Molaro geometry sizes the centre separation d so the t = 0
# neck matches the experiment's first measurement, 32.81 um. That is the right
# thing for reproducing their neck-vs-time curve, and the wrong thing for
# measuring a growth EXPONENT, because it starts the run at r/R = 0.19 and ends
# it at 0.38: less than a factor two, entirely outside the small-neck regime
# where any Kuczynski exponent is derived, and -- see below -- at or under this
# discretisation's resolution floor for the whole run.
#
# Measured on the committed union-IC runs
# (studies/sinter_exponent/verification/molaro_fits.csv): the model's local
# log-slope climbs monotonically from 0.02 to 0.12 over the full 2 h and is
# still rising at the end. The run never leaves the fillet-rounding transient,
# so there is no power law to fit. The three eps arms lie on top of each other,
# which says that is a property of the initial condition, not of the mesh.
#
# This file removes the pre-formed neck: d = R0 + R1 exactly, so the grains
# touch at a point and, under -ic_grain_union 1, the initial neck is ZERO.
# What it buys is the ability to ask whether OUR model produces the same
# exponent at Molaro's grain size as at Demmenie's 1 mm -- Kuczynski scaling
# says m should not depend on R, and that is worth checking rather than
# assuming, since it is the only thing that lets the two studies be compared.
#
#   d = R0 + R1 = 7.25e-5 + 1.01e-4 = 1.735e-4     (pre-necked geometries:
#                                                   1.7028e-4 union,
#                                                   1.7133e-4 additive)
#
# Everything else -- R0, R1, eps, pad, axisym, the union IC -- is identical to
# molaro_2D_L384um_eps0.35um_axisym_T-20pair_union.opts, the STRICT arm, so the
# two are directly comparable and the only variable is the initial neck.
#
# EXPECT A NARROW WINDOW ANYWAY
# -----------------------------
# The neck fillet has radius rho ~ r^2/(2R), resolved only once rho exceeds the
# ~6*eps visible band, i.e. r/R >= sqrt(12*eps/R). At eps = 3.479e-7 and
# R_ave = 86.75 um that floor is
#
#     r/R = 0.219,  i.e. a neck WIDTH of 38.1 um
#
# so this run only becomes measurable ABOVE the experiment's starting neck.
# That is not a defect of the run, it is the finding: at Molaro's grain size
# this model cannot resolve the small-neck regime at any eps it can afford, and
# the exponent has to be measured on the 1 mm geometry (floor 0.087) instead.
# Reaching a useful window needs the neck to roughly double past the floor,
# hence t_final = 8 h in the paired experiment file rather than their 2 h.
#
# CAVEAT INHERITED FROM THE UNION SERIES
# --------------------------------------
# The sharp union has a zero-radius concave crease at the contact point. No
# diffuse interface can hold it; AC dynamics rounds it to O(eps) within a few
# steps. Expect a fast fillet-rounding transient at the start that is NOT
# sintering, and exclude it from any fit -- the r/R floor above does this
# automatically, since the rounding happens far below it.
#
# MESH — unchanged from the strict union arm apart from Lx growing 3 um with d:
#   Lx = d + R0 + R1 + 2*pad = 3.870e-4   (pad = 2.0e-5, as the whole family)
#   Ly = R1 + pad            = 1.210e-4
#   Nx = ceil(sqrt(2)*Lx/eps) = 1574,  Ny = 492   (~774k nodes)
#
# Measure with: python postprocess/neck_width.py <run_dir> --axisym
# Fit with:     python postprocess/fit_neck_growth.py <run_dir>/neck_width.csv --demmenie
# =============================================================================

-axisym 1
-ic_grain_union 1                       # zero neck at tangency — load-bearing

-ic_type multi_grains
-dim 2
-Lx 3.87000e-04
-Ly 1.21000e-04
-Lz 0

-ice_grain_cx 9.25000e-05,2.66000e-04   # d = 1.735e-4 = R0+R1, EXACTLY TANGENT
-ice_grain_cy 0.0,0.0
-ice_grain_R  7.25e-5,1.01e-4
-ice_grain_ax 7.25e-5,1.01e-4
-ice_grain_ay 7.25e-5,1.01e-4

-Nx 1574                                # h = eps/sqrt(2)  (~774k nodes)
-Ny 492
-Nz 1
-eps 3.4790e-07
-eps_valid_temp -20

-delt_t 1.0e-4
-periodic 0
